 dudley do right and on the tv series  home improvement barless and arrested  development he hasn't acted on screen  since 2004 having moved into a career as  a writer with his brother todd von  hoffman the former actor wrote two  humorous pop culture compendiums big  damn book of sheer manliness and bigger  damer book of sheer manliness  chief of police in the unidentified city  of police academy and then later police  commissioner henry hurst is the  institutional antagonist of the  franchise at least initially he's  adamantly against his mayor's idea to  open up the police academy to a wider  variety of candidates he hatches the  plan to make them all quit but after it  doesn't work comes to appreciate the new  cadets the acting career of george r  robertson is notable for two things  portraying henry hurst in six police  academy movies between 1984 and 1989 and  for playing politicians both fictional  and real robertson was president davis  in senior trip senator barry goldwater  in the reagans and vice president dick  cheney in the path to 9 11. robertson  stopped taking on as many roles when he  reached his 80s with one of his last  roles coming in the series haven  cadet george martin's main arc as an  officer isn't one of finding a job or  personal purpose but one of romance he's  ditching his relentless pursuit of as  many young women as possible in order to  get together with trainer debbie  callahan andrew rubin was a seasoned  character actor by the time he played  cadet george martin in the first police  academy a career peak that followed  stints on 70s tv shows like mary hartman  mary hartman swat the odd couple shazam  and the jeffersons after police academy  reuben landed main cast parts on the  short-lived drama series hometown and  joe bash then walked away from acting  for about a decade to head up multiple  non-profit and humanitarian  organizations in 2015 ruben died of lung  cancer at the age of 69 according to the  hollywood reporter the main bad guy of  the original police academy movie is  never given a name instead he's a common  intimidating leather jacket and beanie  clad street thug caricature officially  listed in the credits as main bad guy  the part of main bad guy was played by  prolific character actor and bit player  doug lennox who returned to the series  in police academy 3 back in training to  portray axe murder he notched a few  dozen credits in his time most notably  popping up in x-men lars and the real  girl and against the ropes he appeared  in numerous television shows produced in  his native canada including my secret  identity night heat top cops and due  south also a radio host and an author  lennox died in 2015 at age 77.  violet factler knows that her husband  doug has a tendency to slip up and  create mayhem in one memorable scene  from the first police academy she jumps  on the hood of her husband's car to  prevent him from driving to the academy  sign ups only to get hurt in the process  police academy is an iconic 80s movie  and debra lee scott was an iconic  television personality in her day she  made frequent appearances on the  celebrity powered game shows of the era  including family feud match game and  password plus as a young actor she  appeared on the love boat had a  recurring role on welcome back cotter  and she also played the title  character's sister kathy shumway on the  soap spoof mary hartman mary hartman  scott's career came to an end not long  after she reprised the role of violet  fackler in 1986's police academy 3 back  in training she focused on her personal  life and became engaged to new york city  police officer dennis levi who died at  the world trade center during the 9 11  terrorist attacks according to contact  music scott's family reported that the  tragedy sent the retired actor into a  depression that led her to drink heavily  which resulted in cirrhosis of the liver  scott died in april 2005 at age 52.  check out one of our newest videos righ